celld patch 0004: packs, the transport of Dolt remotes between cells.

Why. DoltLite's remote machinery moves chunks between a store and a remote
that is a file (file://) or an HTTP server. A celld cell is neither: it is one
file owned by one node, written by one owner, and the cell that wants its
history may be on another node. The engine's fetch needs only four things from
a remote (the refs, the chunks it asks for by hash, a presence test), so the
transport can be any request and response, as long as the chunks of one
request are enough for the walk.

What. Three SQL functions, none of which touches the network or a file.

  dolt_pack_build(branches, haves) -> BLOB
    The sender's half. branches is a newline-separated list of "name" or
    "name=sent-as"; haves a list of commit hashes the receiver holds. Returns
    the refs of those branches (commits only: no working sets, tags, remotes
    or tracking refs, so nothing uncommitted or local leaves the store) and
    every chunk of their history that the haves do not cover, found with the
    trusted-set walk that fetch validation already uses.

  dolt_pack_fetch(remote, pack) -> text
    The receiver's half. Opens the pack as a read-only DoltliteRemote and runs
    the engine's own doltliteFetchInto for every branch it carries, into the
    remote-tracking branches remote/<branch>: every chunk is hashed, the graph
    is checked before a tracking ref is installed, and the install is one
    ordinary refs commit. Registered unscoped, like dolt_fetch.

  dolt_pack_haves() -> text
    The commits this store holds under a name (branches, tags, tracking
    branches), for a sender to leave out.

